CLASS:: SwarmInstruments
summary:: Ready-to-use additive pitched instruments and a swarm kick
categories:: Libraries>SwarmSynth
related:: Classes/SwarmInstrument, Classes/SwarmSynthDefs, Classes/SwarmAudition

DESCRIPTION::
SwarmInstruments is a collection of small, reusable additive instruments built
on code::\swarm_partial::. It is independent of any composition. Construction
does not boot a server, install a SynthDef, create a group, or play sound.

Each call to code::make:: returns a fresh SwarmInstrument with its own
SwarmMath state and lazily created playback. The code::natural::,
code::soft::, and code::bright:: variants retain the same partial ratios and
counts while changing spectral weights and partial envelope times. Their
weights sum to code::amp:: per base frequency across all variations; this is not a
claim of equal perceived loudness. Chords add one budget per base frequency;
reduce code::amp:: for large chords. Reducing the partial count removes modes
and lowers the total budget; increasing it adds silent partials.

Flute and clarinet use harmonic and odd-harmonic spectra respectively; organ
emphasizes octaves and fifths. Marimba uses modes at 1:4:10. Bell uses modes at
0.5:1:1.2:1.5:2:3 and is a generic bell approximation, with its supplied pitch
as a reference rather than its lowest mode.

Kick uses code::\swarm_kick:: and defaults to 55 Hz and 0.4 seconds. Its
code::natural:: recipe is a deep electronic hit; code::rough:: adds per-partial
detuning and stronger saturation; code::acoustic:: uses inharmonic modes with
different decay times. Recipe weights are normalized before the amplitude
budget is applied. Public duration, attack, detune, sweep ratio, sweep time,
and drive controls affect the next trigger; private per-partial scales retain
each recipe's independent envelopes and pitch motion.

Flute, clarinet, and organ are gate-sustained instruments. Marimba, bell, and kick
are self-freeing strikes whose next trigger may overlap an earlier tail.
All instruments use centered pan, deterministic phase, one variation, and
the code::\mute:: Nyquist policy by default.

Before playback, boot the server and explicitly call
code::SwarmSynthDefs.install::. Recompile the SuperCollider class library
after installing or changing SwarmSynth classes.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: names
Returns the six collection names in stable order: code::flute::,
code::clarinet::, code::organ::, code::marimba::, code::bell::, and code::kick::.

METHOD:: variants
Returns a defensive copy of the named instrument's complete recipe dictionary.
Pitched instruments expose code::natural::, code::soft::, and code::bright::;
kick exposes code::natural::, code::rough::, and code::acoustic::.

argument:: name
One of the symbols returned by code::names::.

METHOD:: metadata
Returns a defensive metadata copy for an instrument.

The metadata includes code::label::, suggested code::register:: as a MIDI-note
pair, code::articulation::, code::description::, code::auditionGate::,
code::releaseKey::, code::releaseTime::, code::defaultNyquistPolicy::, and an
empty code::descriptors:: array. For struck sounds, code::releaseTime::
provides the longest variant tail allowance for single-note auditions. Suggested registers are musical guidance,
not pitch limits.

argument:: name
One of the symbols returned by code::names::. An unknown name raises an error.

METHOD:: make
Creates a fresh SwarmInstrument. No state or playback is shared with any other
result from this method.

argument:: name
One of the symbols returned by code::names::.

argument:: freqs
One or more positive base frequencies in Hz. Defaults to code::#[440]:: for
pitched instruments and code::#[55]:: for kick.

argument:: amp
Amplitude budget for each base frequency. Defaults to code::0.1::.

argument:: variant
Initial timbre variant. Pitched instruments accept code::\natural::,
code::\soft::, or code::\bright::. Kick accepts code::\natural::,
code::\rough::, or code::\acoustic::. Defaults to code::\natural::.

EXAMPLES::

subsection:: Construction and playback

code::
// Construction is inert.
~flute = SwarmInstruments.make(\flute, #[440], 0.06);
~flute.synth; // nil until the first play

s.waitForBoot {
    SwarmSynthDefs.install;
    s.sync;

    // Event pitch resolution remains available.
    ~flute.play((midinote: 69, gate: 1));
};

// A held instrument must receive gate 1 on every new articulation.
~flute.closeGate;
~flute.play((midinote: 72, transpose: -12, amp: 0.04, gate: 1));
~flute.setVariant(\bright, transitionTime: 0.35);
~flute.closeGate;
~flute.dispose;
::

subsection:: Chords and struck tails

code::
(
~organ = SwarmInstruments.make(\organ, [48, 55, 60, 64].midicps, 0.025, \soft);
~bell = SwarmInstruments.make(\bell, #[440], 0.045);

s.waitForBoot {
    SwarmSynthDefs.install;
    s.sync;

    ~organ.play((gate: 1));

    // Bell uses next-trigger playback. The second strike creates new nodes
    // while the first strike's self-freeing tails continue to decay.
    ~bell.play((midinote: 72));
    { ~bell.play((midinote: 79)) }.defer(0.18);
};
)

// Release removes sound immediately; dispose also removes owned playback.
~organ.closeGate;
~organ.dispose;
~bell.release;
~bell.dispose;
::

subsection:: Listening and audition examples

code::
// See examples/standard-instruments.scd for phrases and variant comparisons.
// See examples/standard-instruments-audition.scd for local registry ownership
// and the SwarmAudition GUI. The GUI clears tails on retrigger for isolation;
// use the listening example for overlapping SwarmInstrument strikes.
::

subsection:: Kick controls

code::
~kick = SwarmInstruments.make(\kick, amp: 0.1);
~kick.play; // natural / Deep Electronic at 55 Hz
~kick.setVariant(\rough);
~kick.play((freq: 48, duration: 0.5, drive: 5));
~kick.setVariant(\acoustic);
~kick.play((attack: 0.004, sweepRatio: 2.4, sweepTime: 0.03));
~kick.dispose;
// See examples/kick.scd and output/kick/ for offline listening renders.
::
